<title>USA: U.S. M-2 money supply up $3.9 bln in July 21 wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. M-2 money supply up $3.9 bln in July 21 wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. M-2 money supply rose $3.9 billion in the July 21 week to $3,931.0 billion, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>The broader M-3 measure rose $2.7 billion to $5,141.5 billion. M-1 was up $900 million to $1,059.4 billion, the Fed said.</p>
<p>The Fed said the four-week moving average of M-2 was $3,930.2 billion versus $3,927.9 billion in the previous week.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
